# gcc64/SOURCES -- every upstream source the gcc64 chain uses past stage 0.
#
# One line per file:   NAME  SHA256  URL [URL ...]
#
#   NAME    the file's name in the cache ($GCC64_CACHE, default
#           build-out/gcc64-cache).  run-gcc64.sh never uses a cached file
#           whose sha256 is not SHA256; it fails loudly instead.
#   SHA256  of the cached file itself (for the git export: of the
#           uncompressed tar, which `git archive` reproduces exactly).
#   URL     tried in order until one gives the right bytes:
#             http(s)://...          the file itself
#             http(s)://...!MEMBER   the file is MEMBER inside that tarball
#                                    (Ubuntu's gcc orig tarballs wrap gcc's own)
#             git+https://REPO#REF@COMMIT:PREFIX
#                                    a shallow clone of REPO at tag/branch REF,
#                                    which must be COMMIT, then
#                                    `git archive --format=tar --prefix=PREFIX/ HEAD`
#
# The first URL is the upstream one live-bootstrap uses (b1ceced7,
# steps/*/sources) whenever our file is byte-identical to live-bootstrap's.
# The Ubuntu archive URL after it is the one actually used to build the
# canonical run: this sandbox's egress policy blocks kernel.org, gnu.org,
# sourceware.org and musl.libc.org.  Where Ubuntu ships the upstream tarball
# unchanged ("= lb" below) the sha256 equals live-bootstrap's.
#
# Also used, from this repo and pinned elsewhere: tcc-0.9.27 (pnut's vendored
# kit/tcc-0.9.27.tar.gz, sha256 db0a0bf3..., checked by
# tests/pnut/sf-pnut-amd64-check.sh) and portable_libc (vendor/pnut at
# commit abc34a5, checked by the same script), both via stage 0's kit.

